WEBVTT

00:04:29.149 --> 00:04:30.428
as a participant,

00:04:30.452 --> 00:04:32.610
we would have calibrated
the difficulty level

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.717
of the puzzles to your expertise.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:37.066
Because we want
these puzzles to be difficult.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.305
These are tricky puzzles,

00:04:38.329 --> 00:04:40.843
because your first instinct
is to say "tulip."

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.307
And then you have to unstick yourself.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.111
Right?

00:04:45.135 --> 00:04:47.850
So these have been calibrated
to your level of expertise,

00:04:47.874 --> 00:04:49.731
because we want this to be difficult,

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.925
and I'll tell you why, momentarily.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:53.680
Now, here's another example.

00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:56.266
Anyone? This is much more difficult.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.306
Audience member: Embark.
BS: Yeah. Wow! OK.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.205
So, yeah, so this is, again, difficult.